@startuml
title D04 - Integration through existing frame and UID publication
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam maxMessageSize 60
autonumber

participant "Existing world task" as World
participant "A: DTAL builder/cache" as Builder
participant "Source producer tasks" as Producers
participant "Existing view/frame task" as Frame
participant "Existing LightManager" as Manager
participant "Existing ClusterLightLists" as Clusters
participant "Existing RHI / GPU" as GPU

opt DTAL regeneration requested
  World -> Builder : capture safe inputs; build temporary data
  Builder -> Builder : validate geometry, PDFs, budgets and revision
  Builder -> Manager : install complete group generation
  Manager -> GPU : replacement copies / descriptors / safe retirement
end

Producers -> Frame : completed source producer results
World -> Frame : world data ready
Frame -> Manager : current accepted parents and group emission
Frame -> Clusters : generic UID / bounds / reach / coverage / power
alt Project B enabled
  Clusters -> Clusters : update affected candidates and fast / tail tables
else Existing policy
  Clusters -> Clusters : compose existing capped source lists
end
Clusters -> Manager : publish CPU source UID tables
Manager -> Manager : resolve UIDs to current frame indices
Manager -> GPU : publish matching indices / probabilities and barriers
Frame -> GPU : dispatch direct and indirect consumers
GPU -> GPU : select parent then sample real member / point

note over Manager,GPU
  Existing frame slots keep compatible resource data.
  Array-order changes refresh index publication.
  Retirement waits for actual GPU use, not only CPU tasks.
end note
@enduml
